Okay, where to begin... Well, I didn't take notes, and I took a long
break from playing in the middle of the game, so my memory is a bit
sketchy, especially in the early game. Some events may be written here
in the wrong order. Also, please excuse any sentence fragments and
switches to the present tense that I failed to catch. Anyway, at some
point early on, I successfully dipped for Excalibur. When I went to
sokoban, I at first tried to do it without spoilers. Big mistake. I had
to do a lot of scroll-reading and boulder-smashing to fix my mistakes...
After that fiasco, I consulted spoilers for the rest. The zoo contained
a bag of holding, but ironically, I had already found one on the first
level of sokoban. Bleah. At some point after that, I got my big break:
In a chest was a wand of wishing at 0:3! But alas, "Unfortunately,
nothing happens!" Oops, all that mucking about in sokoban must have
killed my luck! I waited until I was sure my luck was positive, after
throwing what gems I had at unicorns. I think I wished for: gauntlets of
power, silver dragon scale mail, cloak of magic resistance, boots of
speed, helm of brilliance (all blessed, plussed, and fooproofed, of
course), and the 2 blessed scrolls of charging. Also, at some point, I
found and identified an amulet of life saving. Now I was all kitted up,
but I still didn't have a luckstone... When I went to the bottom of the
mines, I kick-tested a gray stone. Okay, it moved, let's pick it up...
Wha? Loadstone?? *slaps forehead* Note to self: REMOVE gauntlets of
power BEFORE kick-testing! I quickly consulted a spoiler to find the
location of the real stone, and I started going back up. Now, at this
point, I had found NO altars except for the cross-aligned minetown one,
and neither had I found and holy water. So, guess who was next on my
hit-list... At the minetown altar, I initiated an unprovoked attack
against the priest, but not before donating all my gold to him ;).
Suddenly I was Overtaxed? It took me a couple of turns to figure out
that it was my bag of holding that got cursed. Grah! I dropped it and
slaughtered the priest mercilessly. I converted the altar, but all the
water was in my bag... I had no choice, I opened the bag and took out
what I needed. I think nothing important vanished. Anyway, I prayed on
the altar and got the holy water. I uncursed, then blessed my bag,
uncursed my loadstone, and blessed my luckstone. I was now wearing an
amulet of ESP to make up for my lost telepathy, but I eventually found a
floating eye. At the lower levels, suddenly there were altars (grr). At
level 21, there was an altar which I used to set up a stash. I can't
remember anything else eventful happening now until I got to Medusa's
level, which was the one with the big island in the middle. I chucked
rocks at the sea critters until they died, then crossed the water with a
ring of levitation. Medusa took one look at my armor and turned to
stone. Perseus had the silver shield, not that I needed one. On a level
below, there was a polymorph trap. I used a scroll to tame some monster.
I displaced it onto the trap a lot, but eventually it turned into a long
worm, which I couldn't displace. Bleah. When I got to the castle (for
the first time), I masterminded the passtune. I used my amulet of ESP
again so I could see the monsters in the moat while doing this, and
polearm them to death when necessary. Once I got the passtune, I smashed
and crushed until there were no Liches left. Then I slaughtered the rest
of the inhabitants by hand. I got the wand, but I didn't use it
immediately. I put it in my bag. I started to return to my stash. On the
way up, I found a horse and tamed it. I had found a magic whistle in the
castle, and I used it to polymorph the horse on the polymorph trap.
First try, a cockatrice. I decided not to push my luck and moved on.
When I returned to my stash, I contemplated a change of equipment. I
liked the extrinsic telepathy, but I wanted to be able to wear an amulet
of life saving. I also had a mind to be a spellcaster, now that I had
found a robe, so I needed something else to give me magic resistance. I
reviewed my options in a spoiler and opted for the Orb of Detection. I
used two wishes on it. I also wished for gauntlets of dexterity , a
t-shirt, and a magic marker.  This left the wand at 1:0. I saved the
last wish for later. I used the magic marker to enchant my stuff. Now, I
still hadn't done the quest, so I did it. Fortunately, on the last level
of the quest, one of Ashikaguy's minions had a wand of death, which I
used on him. I brought the loot back up and returned to my base. Now
that I was going to be a spellcaster, I needed spellbooks. So, I went
all around the dungeon gathering all the heavy spellbooks I left behind,
as well as potions and anything I might want for polypiling. I also
found a magic marker in the mines. I returned to my base and started
polypiling scrolls, wands, and rings. I wanted scrolls of genocide,
wands of cancellation, and a ring of teleport control (more on that
later). I got these, including 5 scrolls of geno (!). I used up the
wands of cancellation on making blank scrolls and water. I also
alchemized full healing. I quaffed all but two, which was I think 14
potions. That brought my HP up a LOT. The genocides went on L, h, and ;
just for the heck of it. Now, one thing on my to do list was to get
teleport control. So, I confused-remove cursed some water, used some
unholy water to curse the scrolls, and set about reverse genociding
tengus. The ring of teleport control I got earlier was in case I failed
to get TC. I had to write geno once because my first two scrolls failed
to get me TC. Finally, on the second-last tengu, I got it. Hooray! Now,
still on my list was spellbooks. I didn't have the really good spells
that I wanted. I went up again, and on a level with an altar I
encountered a black pudding. Several thousand turns of pudding farming
later, I had the spellbooks I wanted, as well as a couple of useless
artifacts and some more hitpoints. I should also mention that I used
surplus scrolls of gold detection and potions of object detection to try
to find the portal to ludios, but I couldn't even find a vault in the
range where the portal could appear. So now I returned to my stash.
Somewhere along the lines, I lost my protection. I must have prayed once
too often or something... So, I gathered all my money and went down to
the valley of the dead and donated there. I was able to recover 5 of my
original 10 points of protection. I went down, down into gehennom. My
cockatrice got disintegrated by a black dragon. Curse you, black dragon!
That was the longest-lived pet I ever had! I forget when exactly, but I
went back up.  I returned to my stash. Now, I had encountered a few
succubi, but it wasn't safe for me to, uh, use their services. I still
wasn't level 30, so I used my last wish on a blessed +2 ring of
adornment. It came out at +0, so I had to use a scroll of charging,
which got it to +3. I had also jumped on some magic traps on my way up
from gehennom to boost my charisma. Now I went down, down again. I could
cast magic mapping now at something like 90% failure with the robe on,
but it still helped. Along the way, I used up the succubi. Down some
more.  I found vlad's tower. Up, up. I stepped on a bear trap. Hmm, I
have the spell of jumping, let's see what happens... *RRRIP* Oops. I put
on a ring of levitation while my leg healed because I was now burdened
without it. And my leg took a LONG TIME to heal. Anyways, I killed vlad
and got the candelabrum. Go down again, find vibrating square, drop
candelabrum. There was a succubus, and she got me to level 30. I then
went back up to my stash. I got ready to kill Rodney. I got out and ID'd
all the wands of death I found, and I got the bell of opening. I went
down again and killed rodney. Along the way I tamed a purple worm. I
went down to the VS and.. wait... I forgot to bring the candles!
Gnashing of teeth! I go back up again (controlled teleport helps with
all this going up and down). Rodney appeared once in Orcus-town. He was
death-zapped. I went back up and grabbed 7 candles from the stash. I
cursed teleported back down, performed the invocation, and went down to
the sanctum. I killed the priest and laughed at Moloch's lightning
bolts. I got the amulet and named it. Now I began the long journey back
up. Along the way, my purple worm ate a chameleon and turned into... a
woodchuck. Ooo, useful. I left him behind and continued. I must have got
pulled down below Jubilex's swamp 3 times. I finally made it back out
and returned to the stash. I got out my supplies for the ascension run.
Up, up, up, up, up... Finally arrived at the stairs. I checked my
equipment again, then went up... and zapped Rodney to death. I
confused-read gold detection and dug to the portal, which was close.
Earth was severely uneventful. On Air, I put on my ring of levitation.
Now I saw why people hate air elementals so much. I alternated between
killing them normally and zapping them with wands of death. They got me
down to about half my HP, so I quaffed a potion of full healing. I
confused-detected the portal and moved on. On fire, I confuse-detected
the portal again and levitated over the lava. Gah, you stupid monsters,
stop breathing fire. Eventually I made it to the portal. Water was
undoubtedly the plane I spent the most time on. I had an amulet of
magical breathing, but I didn't want to get the stuff in my bags wet. I
fell into the water once because I forgot to un-confuse myself, but
fortunately my bags were greased. I re-greased them and started
wandering around the bubbles, trying to get closer to the portal. I used
the Orb of Detection 3 times, but it didn't help much, especially since
the bubbles moved AFTER I saw where the portal was. Eventually I saw a
cobra vanish, so I knew I was close. I wandered a bit more and stumbled
into the portal... On Astral, I promptly put on a ring of conflict and
dispatched the resulting angels. Famine was in the middle, so I satiated
myself and went that way. I killed him and cleared a path to the altar
with wands of teleport/death. The altar was chaotic. I zapped my way
back and went left. Pestilence was there. I killed him without getting
sick. I zapped my way through again and the altar was lawful. Yippee!
Hooray! Callooh! Callay! ahem...

